# ── Booking ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The form POSTs here when someone sends a booking. It must be the /exec URL
# of the Apps Script web app in scripts/booking-endpoint.gs:
#
#   https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfy.../exec
#
# A spreadsheet URL (docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/...) is the DOCUMENT, not
# an endpoint — it cannot receive a POST. The site checks the shape and ignores
# anything that is not an /exec URL, so a wrong value degrades to "WhatsApp
# only" rather than failing a booking. Which of the two happened is shown on
# the confirmation screen, and warned about in the browser console.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means this ships in the page source. That is fine: the URL is
# not a secret, and the Google credential stays inside the Apps Script.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_ENDPOINT=

# ── Content push (local only — never NEXT_PUBLIC_) ───────────────────────
# `npm run content:push` writes data/content.xlsx tabs to the Google content
# sheet through the endpoint above. Must equal CONTENT_TOKEN in the Apps
# Script's Script Properties.
CONTENT_WRITE_TOKEN=

# ── Admin references (not used by the site) ──────────────────────────────
# The sheet ids are already compiled into scripts/booking-endpoint.gs. These
# are just handy links to the live sheets.
# BOOKINGS_SHEET_URL=
# PEOPLE_SHEET_URL=
# CONTENT_SHEET_URL=
